  "gaps": [
    "Catalog year/term is not stated (the only dated reference is the tuition period 'Fall '26 - Summer '27').",
    "The credit unit is not explicitly labeled; semester credits are inferred from references to '15-week semester' and 'credit hours'.",
    "No residency/institutional-credit requirement is tied to specific courses; the page only says 'CCO accepts up to 90 transfer credits toward a bachelor's degree'.",
    "MATH 190 appears both as a Professional Course and as a Quantitative Literacy option; the capture does not say whether one course may satisfy both requirements.",
    "Several courses (COMM 130, COMM 140, CRIT 220, PHIL 240, MKCM 120) appear under more than one General Education category; the double-counting policy is not stated.",
    "CSCI 410 lists MATH-160 Logic and Probability as a prerequisite, so the Quantitative Literacy choice may effectively be MATH 160; the capture does not state this as a requirement.",
    "Prerequisites reference CMIT-235 Advanced Python as an alternative to SDEV-340, but CMIT 235 is not listed in the curriculum.",
    "Minimum GPA for graduation, upper-level credit minimums, and any minimum grades in major courses are not stated.",
    "Course options for the 6-credit General Education Elective are given by subject prefix only; no specific course list is provided."
  ],
